From e3c63ffda0e856a656193831b6fab2ee565a6334 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 07:02:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] always-on: drain keep-alive sockets before a
 superseded backend retires

Desktop's keep-alive sockets stay pinned to a superseded blue/green backend
through the TCP-splice proxy; retiring it with them open hung up every in-flight
request at once (hub 06:47:16Z Nov 13: 9/9 keep-alive connections dropped), and
on the MacBook a hang-up tears down and redials the hub SSH transport.

While superseded, every HTTP response now carries Connection: close, so each
pinned socket closes after its next response and the next request goes to the
active backend. The superseded watchdog asks the idle fence only after >= 8 s
superseded with no open uvicorn HTTP connection (WebSockets excluded), or at a
30 s cap; an aborted roll stops the drain. Fence and reaper unchanged.

Card t_01a1d09123dbb9c4.
